From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:11:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor: Suppress manual driver bind
 and unbind

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

The ACPI processor driver is tied to CPU-hotplug ownership. Manually
unbinding it can remove an online CPU's cpuidle device and hierarchical
power-domain consumer while the CPU continues to execute, violating
shared-state coordination. A later manual bind is not a safe reconstruction
transaction either.

Suppress the driver-core bind and unbind attributes. Physical CPU and
module lifecycle paths continue to use the coordinated teardown and rebuild
machinery.

Co-developed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9830cedcd5879b254b399a436088914f30a01b0f resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00641
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@c7d60555d1061d543c8183c326d0edf464779e60
---
 drivers/acpi/processor_driver.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/processor_driver.c b/drivers/acpi/processor_driver.c
index 940b553f3e4b..5a5e1113a19d 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/processor_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/processor_driver.c
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, processor_device_ids);
 static struct device_driver acpi_processor_driver = {
 	.name = "processor",
 	.bus = &cpu_subsys,
+	.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
 	.acpi_match_table = processor_device_ids,
 	.remove = acpi_processor_stop,
 };
